{"name":"Haggis","hex":"#c3c7b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Haggis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Haggis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Haggis","blocks":[{"text":"Haggis is a savoury pudding and sausage containing sheep's pluck, minced with chopped onion, oatmeal, suet, seasonings, and salt, mixed with stock, and cooked while traditionally encased in the animal's stomach though now an artificial casing is often used instead. According to the 2001 English edition of the Larousse Gastronomique: \"Although its description is not immediately appealing, haggis has an excellent nutty texture and delicious savoury flavour\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Scotland_Haggis.jpg/330px-Scotland_Haggis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haggis","wikidata":"Q209500"},{"title":"Haggis (programming language)","blocks":[{"text":"Haggis is a high-level reference programming language used primarily to examine computing science for Scottish pupils taking SQA courses on the subject. Haggis is used as a tool to bridge the gap between pseudocode and typical computer programming."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haggis_(programming_language)","wikidata":"Q28404924"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg/500px-Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg/1280px-Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg/500px-Haggis_on_a_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haggis on a platter at